<h2 class="sec">Purpose</h2>
<p class="body">Test your Sprint 2 learning by applying what you learned in three real-world situations where it can be applied, and identify two similar looking situations where the quantitative relationship doesn't hold because the physical condition is different.</p>

<h2 class="sec">How this form works</h2>
<p class="body">In week 8 you stated in words what you start from and what you want to predict. This week you take that goal from words to working physics in three steps:</p>
<ul class="tlist body" style="margin-bottom:14px">
<li><b>Step 1 (Part 1):</b> Use your learning resource or a simulation to understand the mathematical formula (quantitative relationship), check it once, and state the physical condition where it is applicable.</li>
<li><b>Step 2 (Part 2):</b> Work the numbers step by step across three real situations where that condition holds.</li>
<li><b>Step 3 (Part 3):</b> Take a working situation and change one physical detail so that the setup looks the same on the surface, but the formula is not applicable.</li>
</ul>

